            {
                "entry_id": "643029d3-55b0-30a4-8abb-b28f3943c742",
                "word": "mog",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "26f3b120-236d-4ef9-8cd2-ef1cfb9a1ebb",
                        "entry_id": "643029d3-55b0-30a4-8abb-b28f3943c742",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mogs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "101d8825-17c4-3ef6-92a8-704b0ffd4540",
                        "entry_id": "643029d3-55b0-30a4-8abb-b28f3943c742",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A cat."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc938241-2dbf-4617-a9e7-6a724ec11e3e",
                                "sense_id": "101d8825-17c4-3ef6-92a8-704b0ffd4540",
                                "text": "Get that mog out of here!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c636c3d8-826f-4fdb-9845-3e1f00299a26",
                                "sense_id": "101d8825-17c4-3ef6-92a8-704b0ffd4540",
                                "text": "The more I hear about Larry the Downing Street cat, the more his story becomes an allegory for our time. As previously reported, the reputation of this mog was trashed by Downing Street spin doctors after he was brought in to clear the Prime Minister’s workplace of mice in 2011."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56a8be6a-4a1d-47f5-aba7-f25b8472c443",
                                "sense_id": "101d8825-17c4-3ef6-92a8-704b0ffd4540",
                                "text": "Ulysses the cat is the real breakout star of the Coen brothers' Inside Llewyn Davis. He's not the first feline scene-stealer, though - here are ten other great cats in film (animated mogs excluded)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae82f85d-91ab-48a4-8bdb-4e4477eca909",
                                "sense_id": "101d8825-17c4-3ef6-92a8-704b0ffd4540",
                                "text": "A few months before she died, Winefride had started setting food out for a brindled mog named Sally who lived in their neighborhood. She was always feeding local cats, but she especially loved this mog, and eventually, Sally grew enormous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "316467ac-e540-46dc-b6ba-296fa82bac6c",
                                "sense_id": "101d8825-17c4-3ef6-92a8-704b0ffd4540",
                                "text": "They two gorgeous mogs even have their own teddy bear and blanket to make their snuggling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65f8f1c7-a3ca-4f65-bd59-0e39245f345d",
                                "sense_id": "101d8825-17c4-3ef6-92a8-704b0ffd4540",
                                "text": "Many pet owners have taken up cat-walking in recent years, encouraged by others on social media and by the growing range of outdoorsy cat kit on offer. But for most mogs, the RSPCA suggests, \"an indoor environment with plenty of opportunities to be active and mentally stimulated is likely to be more beneficial for the cat's welfare than walking them on a lead.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "5233f836-7e07-3db2-a4cb-b3d97a1b89db",
                "word": "mog",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cc6e7d22-34d5-4379-a42a-7faf516a714a",
                        "entry_id": "5233f836-7e07-3db2-a4cb-b3d97a1b89db",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "mogs"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ca66d348-8c19-4c95-94c1-b7634f766e23",
                        "entry_id": "5233f836-7e07-3db2-a4cb-b3d97a1b89db",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "mogging"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1a92bbc4-d6e6-4d4d-949c-f8f629bbd4cc",
                        "entry_id": "5233f836-7e07-3db2-a4cb-b3d97a1b89db",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "mogged"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8e2d98ea-7a8d-4afc-bc5c-c216b77130b8",
                        "entry_id": "5233f836-7e07-3db2-a4cb-b3d97a1b89db",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "mogged"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe3b4a0c-6c02-37ee-a577-42e5bbb8ae48",
                        "entry_id": "5233f836-7e07-3db2-a4cb-b3d97a1b89db",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To remove (a public servant) from their position following a Machinery of Government change, a process in which the Government of Australia reorganizes the responsibilities and structure of the government."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "informal",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "68c7d1a5-c312-4937-a948-a3e2cb6e34fc",
                                "sense_id": "fe3b4a0c-6c02-37ee-a577-42e5bbb8ae48",
                                "text": "The slowdown in house purchases prior to an election is natural, but not because public servant buyers are skittish about the political climate. They just don't want to watch the ink dry on their sale on a house in Tuggeranong, close to their department, only to be comprehensively mogged and presented with a commute to another building in faraway Belconnen - or worse, Gosford."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd3a0906-06e3-4a54-908b-abc4207d0541",
                                "sense_id": "fe3b4a0c-6c02-37ee-a577-42e5bbb8ae48",
                                "text": "[Kevin] Rudd, [Peter] Coaldrake and [Glyn] Davis joined [Wayne] Goss, [Tom] Burns and Treasurer Keith De Lacy on the Machinery of Government (MOG) Committee that reviewed the reports of the PSMC (and led to the idiom that people had been 'mogged')."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6fb96185-73e9-4692-be5f-74a21f429c3d",
                                "sense_id": "fe3b4a0c-6c02-37ee-a577-42e5bbb8ae48",
                                "text": "But recently under a machinery of government change, with the centralisation of the cybersecurity function under Alastair MacGibbon, that team has been mogged out from the DTA."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b40aaf3-29e1-4add-a7ed-ac6a06382c9c",
                                "sense_id": "fe3b4a0c-6c02-37ee-a577-42e5bbb8ae48",
                                "text": "After every election there is a lot of focus on the reshuffle – the personnel changes as a prime minister creates their new team. But civil servants will also be looking to see if it is not just their ministerial team who are reshuffled but whether they have been \"mogged\" – the verb the Australians use for what we rather less dramatically call \"subjected to a machinery of government change\". If we read the manifestos, there is quite a lot of potential \"mogging\" on offer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "deffe188-c259-4cbf-b5af-5392f16d8c5b",
                                "sense_id": "fe3b4a0c-6c02-37ee-a577-42e5bbb8ae48",
                                "text": "On Friday night, at the stroke of midnight, over 70,000 Commonwealth workers will be mogged, as the [Scott] Morrison government's abolition of four portfolios officially take effect, with an expected cost of $80 million."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
